Verification applies to this **canonical HTML**, not inherited exploration results. Current offline workspace: installed/built, **96/96 entries** available. Command: `python /home/david/dev/metodologia/skill/scripts/bitacora.py components mockup build <design>/cuentas-admin@v1.r13.dir-a.tsx --out <design>/cuentas-admin@v1.html`. Result: **678 KB, 2150 source files, exit 0**. The immutable exploration was rebuilt directly; only the documented Taller/session corrections and draft inspector label were applied in canonical bundled output. No component dependency installation, network asset fetch or HTML fallback was needed. Final HTML SHA-256: `41de6620ad2ca6f4cdf18177cde91e72868bb70036768259912950a28045204b`.

`python <kit>/kit/contrast.py <design>/cuentas-admin@v1.html`: **158 pairs checked in light and dark, all pass**, exit 0.

`UV_OFFLINE=1 uv run --offline --with playwright python <kit>/kit/audit_mockup.py <design>/cuentas-admin@v1.html --max-combos 476`, with current system `/usr/bin/chromium`: **476 renders / 476 planned combinations**, **12,358 text measurements**, **1,372 focus stops**, exit 0. Every view/state/theme plus dialog scenes at 1280/390px was measured, without sampling omissions.

`RESULT: PASS — no contrast, non-text, focus, alignment, padding or overflow problems`

Supplementary cached-Playwright groups: **414 assertions passed across focused groups**. Five system roles show exactly **3/5/6/9/12** checked grants out of **12**; four tool fieldsets retain the Taller bundle helper. ES/EN own-password feedback renews this browser while administrator-reset feedback still requests sign-in. Consent gates activation; invalid links remove passwords; mandatory notice omits product navigation; invitation Escape restores initiating focus after modal readiness. **112 responsive cases** (seven views × two themes × ES/EN × 360/768/1024/1440px) passed overflow/font checks and, for forms, 676px cap/equal-gutter checks. The selected r13 and canonical composition/motion CSS templates are **byte-identical**. Expressive entrance has **8 running animations**, `?still=1` **0**, OS reduced motion **0**. No browser exceptions or HTTP(S) requests were observed.

Probe history: the first supplementary probe pressed Escape before modal focus readiness and failed its immediate closed assertion. Waiting for the visible dialog and its focus transition confirmed Escape/dismissal/focus return, without changing product code. The responsive follow-up completed all 112 cases, then failed only because its CSS-extraction regex assumed a semicolon after the bundled template; extraction using the actual template boundary confirmed identity. The remaining motion/network checks passed in a focused follow-up. Neither interrupted script is represented as an uninterrupted passing run; completed assertion groups and corrected probes supply the totals above.

Screenshots inspected **in memory**, with no screenshot files: 1280/light login, 1280/dark roles, 390/light login error, 390/dark activation. They retain the selected compact header, centred form axis, rounded surfaces, readable error alignment and wrapping phone identity. Static completion checks cover twelve sections, draft status, forty unique visual criteria, verbatim SPEC notice in both languages and unchanged source hashes.

**Not run:** production lint/types/tests/build, real authentication or server permission checks, durable role/session/token operations, database concurrency, full WCAG certification or legal review. Those belong to later implementation/integration/review tasks. This design task adds no production code and does not attest those checks.


