**Resolved from existing plan:** r13's inherited question about own-password completion is answered by T2.2: end old sessions and issue a new session to this requesting browser. Mi cuenta remains signed in; administrator reset separately returns to login. T1.2 defines 12 permission grants and cumulative system counts 3/5/6/9/12; Taller sub-capabilities are helper copy, not separately grantable permissions. These are corrections to verified discrepancies, not new owner decisions.

**Confirmed:** owner-selected r13 Parte de acceso; production palette and Geist; centred form hierarchy and retained motion; one role per account; five system roles/three cumulative plans; at least one permission for custom roles; eight-character minimum, seven-day invitations, 24-hour resets; admin-generated single-use links without automatic email; newer unused links revoke prior same-kind links; immediate session on activation; generic fifteen-minute login hint; mandatory notice reacceptance; saved-work/last-active-administrator protections.

**Limits:** fixture success demonstrates feedback, not authentication, server routing, durable roles, clipboard delivery, token expiry or legal compliance. The global inspector exposes unrelated state/view combinations for review, not valid product transitions. Role persistence/counts and saved-work eligibility must come from SP-1/T2.2, not fixture list position. Later implementation must verify route focus, pending mutations, stale/offline recovery, screen readers and full keyboard behavior. The product browser-language notice rule remains; this planning artifact deliberately starts ES for owner inspection. No optional production preview is enabled or created.

